IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-enforce`

-- Tests for the hand-gathered route (ss 1, 2 and 7).  Every expected value is written from the texts of ss 1(2), 2(1),
-- 2(3), 2(4) and 7(1) to (5), with the reason beside it, before the module was run.  The inputs are, in order: the
-- restriction of s 1(2) applies; the answer under s 2(1); under s 2(3); under s 2(4); the answers under s 7(1) to (5).

§ `Tests -- the route`

-- nothing bars, the two conditions of s 2(1) are met: may enforce.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no exception in play at all.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- each way to a no`

-- the restriction of s 1(2) bars, whatever else holds.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither route of s 2(1).
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not identified under s 2(3).
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(4): enforcement otherwise than in accordance with the other terms.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- one of the exceptions of s 7 says no (here the second, a company contract).
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (LIST NOTHING, JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- and the last, a carriage contract.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- not answered`

-- a contract of 1 July 2002 without the express provision: the restriction is undecided.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(1) or s 2(3) not stated.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- a no beats an undecided restriction.
#ASSERT `ss 1, 2 and 7 taken together the third party may enforce the term of the contract` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
